00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:04.550 align:start position:0%
the bernanke museum is the second most  visited in greece after the acropolis  museum  it has a collection spanning 2 000 years  of greek  islamic and asian civilization but it's  in financial trouble  70 percent of its income is from ticket  sales restaurants and shops in its nine  venues  the pandemic has forced greece to close  museums drying up that revenue  so the bernanke asked the living artists  it displays  to contribute works for an online  auction  it gathered 240 priced anywhere between  40 euros and 70 000 and the auction it  says is going well  partly thanks to the museum's clean  record of acquisition  contrary to all the major european  museums this is not a colonial museum  which it was built on love for art  and history it was not built as the  outcome of an imperial power colonial  power  that has gathered all these treasures  from around the world the bernanke is  doing  as much online business as it can  shipping gifts ahead of christmas  but the shortfall it has to cover is  considerable  the bernanke museum needs eight and a  half million dollars a year to keep its  doors open  every month that it's closed it loses  half a million dollars  two lockdowns this year have so far kept  its shut  for five months depriving it of almost a  third of its annual income  and that doesn't include company  sponsorships for exhibitions like this  one  which was due to open on the day the  latest lockdown began  but the benagi's board is determined to  succeed  because this is the only museum that  traces  greek identity through all its phases  from antiquity  through byzantium to the modern state  the bernanke became a depository  of trust for the greek society  and also the greeks of the diaspora that  every single time that they had  something important to donate and  preserve for the next generation  they would rather give it to the  bernanke museum the bernanke then  provided  the binary society vision and content  and over the years we had this  relationship of trust  the bernanke is now calling on that  global community of supporters to help  it survive during this challenging time  john saropolos al jazeera athens
 

